taff writer, has uncovered an astonishing trove of documents, including the never-before-seen private papers of Wonder Woman’s creator, William Moulton Marston. The Marston family story is a tale of drama, intrigue, and irony. In the 1920s, Marston and his wife brought into their home Olive Byrne, the niece of Margaret Sanger, one of the most influential feminists of the twentieth century. Even while celebrating conventional family life in a regular column that Marston and Byrne wrote for Family Circle, they themselves pursued lives of extraordinary nonconformity.","pageCount":477,"publicationYear":2015,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"Social Science","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-the-secret-history-of-wonder-woman-jill-lepore"}],"displaySummary":"The Marston family story is a tale of drama, intrigue, and irony. In the 1920s, Marston and his wife brought into their home Olive Byrne, the niece of Margaret Sanger, in a regular column that Marston and Byrne wrote for Family Circle, they themselves pursued lives of extraordinary nonconformity.","primaryTopic":"Gender & Feminism","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Gender & Sexuality","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Gender & Sexuality","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Gender & Sexuality","mappedSubject":"Gender & Sexuality","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book primarily explores the contributions of Wonder Woman to the history of feminism and women's rights while contextualizing it within American history and cultural society.","id":"subject-evidence-book-the-secret-history-of-wonder-woman-jill-lepore-1"},{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","rawLabel":"Social Science","mappedSubject":"Society & Culture","score":5,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-the-secret-history-of-wonder-woman-jill-lepore","id":"subject-evi